SOURCE TEXT
-----------

No authoritative passage text is released. Passage identity is disclosed
through normalized-text SHA-256 digests only, which lets a replicator confirm
they hold the same edition without either party transmitting the text.

The three editions evaluated in Paper 01 are the Berean Standard Bible (public
domain), the World English Bible Updated (public domain), and the Literal
Standard Version (CC BY-SA). Restricted editions were excluded from the primary
phase and require separate authorization.

Public protocol examples use King James Version wording for illustration. Users
outside the United States should verify local rights status before
redistributing any source text.

